.TH "CIRCLECI-MIGRATE" "1" "Jun 2026" "circleci-migrate" "CircleCI Org Migration CLI"

.SH NAME
circleci-migrate-doctor - Run migration preflight checks without migrating.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcircleci-migrate doctor [--source-org ] [--dest-org ] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
doctor runs the same preflight checks as 'migrate' but exits immediately
after printing the summary — it does not export or sync any data.

.PP
Use it to validate your tokens, org slugs, and configuration before running a
migration. It is safe to run as many times as needed; it is entirely read-only.

.PP
If --dest-org is omitted, only source-side checks are run (token present, source
org reachable, api-trigger flag state, and project discovery). If --source-org is
omitted, only destination-side checks are run (token present, destination org
reachable, cross-type warning, GitHub token for repo resolution).

.PP
Exit codes:
  0 — all checks passed (OK or warnings only)
  1 — one or more hard failures (missing required token or unreachable org)

.PP
Examples:
  # Check both source and destination:
  circleci-migrate doctor --source-org gh/acme --dest-org gh/acme-new

.PP
# Source-side only (validate before export):
  circleci-migrate doctor --source-org gh/acme

.PP
# Destination-side only (validate before sync):
  circleci-migrate doctor --dest-org gh/acme-new


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dest-github-org\fP=""
	Destination GitHub organization owner (e.g. 'acme-new'). Use when repos have moved to a new GitHub org. Triggers the GitHub-token check.

.PP
\fB--dest-org\fP=""
	Destination organization slug: gh/ or circleci/\&. When provided, destination-side checks are run (token, reachability, cross-type warning, GitHub token). May be combined with --source-org to run both sides.

.PP
\fB--github-token\fP=""
	GitHub personal access token used to resolve repository IDs when creating pipeline definitions in a GitHub App destination org. Falls back to $GITHUB_TOKEN.

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for doctor

.PP
\fB--source-org\fP=""
	Source organization slug: gh/ or circleci/\&. When provided, source-side checks are run (token, reachability, api-trigger flag, project discovery). May be combined with --dest-org to run both sides.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging

.PP
\fB--dest-token\fP=""
	API token for the destination org (env: CIRCLECI_DEST_TOKEN)

.PP
\fB--host\fP="https://circleci.com"
	CircleCI host URL (env: CIRCLECI_CLI_HOST, CIRCLECI_HOST, or CIRCLE_URL)

.PP
\fB--source-token\fP=""
	API token for the source org (env: CIRCLECI_SOURCE_TOKEN)

.PP
\fB--token\fP=""
	Personal API token — fallback for both orgs (env: CIRCLECI_CLI_TOKEN or CIRCLE_TOKEN)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcircleci-migrate(1)\fP
